0..73 Comment "//! The empty type and the apartness rule. `Empty` is a data type with no"
74..150 Comment "//! constructor, so a match on it has no arm and answers whatever type it is"
151..230 Comment "//! asked for: `A -> Empty` is how \"not A\" is spelled. A path between two terms"
231..308 Comment "//! of a data type is eliminated the same way when the terms are apart: their"
309..387 Comment "//! type\'s rules converge, and their normal forms first differ at two distinct"
388..464 Comment "//! constructors, so no path joins them and a match on one has no arm either"
465..522 Comment "//! [Coquand-1992-pattern_matching_with_dependent_types]."
523..526 Comment "//!"
527..571 Comment "//! - see: #534 — `viaLambda`, `viaStated`"
572..619 Comment "//! - see: #1944 — `viaBare`, `viaBareStated`"
620..675 Comment "//! - see: #1948 — `viaArgument`, `viaArgumentStated`"
676..741 Comment "//! - cites: [Coquand-1992-pattern_matching_with_dependent_types]"
742..745 Comment "//!"
